evidence[8]:
  - Independently verified all 88 subject entries and both accepted snapshot hashes; all unchanged after checks. Exact source base HEAD retained.
  - Safe final JUnit independently confirms 1863 passed, 56 skipped, no failures; every mapped case in all 22 REQ and 24 AC exists with matching result.
  - Through published fixed-allowlist runner, 66 selected existing cases passed independently in 84.53 seconds. Source unchanged, no skips or timeout.
  - Four synthetic sequence probes failed on Bash 3.2.57 and 5.3.20; immediate repeated successful uninstall returns 1 and list reports phantom missing/broken.
  - Two follow-up probes failed on both interpreters; repeated uninstall leaves phase=tools/running journal and blocks later unrelated install fd. Source unchanged in all runs.
  - Independently compared 28 public pin/adapter/production checks to HEAD; all preserved after only allowed nvim metadata normalization. Dots, private Navi adapters and tracked fixture scopes unchanged.
  - No restricted smoke01/02 raw logs/XML/full-trace JSON, older raw captures/private archive, original dev/.env/user.local or actual user config opened or hashed. Earlier subprocess privacy uncertainty remains disclosed and is not negated by this audit.
  - No native Flyline ABI qualification, real picker/Atuin qualification, network/live assets, real host install, startup/global config or actual checkout Git mutations. Safe runner and fixtures read before use.
