findings[2]:
  - id: A0-001
    severity: high
    required: true
    location: "tools/lib/managed/uninstall.sh:22-31, tools/lib/managed/journal.sh:55-83 and common recovery interaction."
    issue: Completed uninstall tombstone receipts become new scope before journal archive removes them; second uninstall creates running item without valid remove receipts and blocks future lifecycle operations.
    evidence: Safe audit-sequences has 2 repeated-uninstall failures; audit-followup has 2 blocked unrelated-install failures on Bash 3.2.57/5.3.20.
    required_result: Treat completed receipts as history for new selection; repeat actual uninstall is readonly no-op 0, later install/update works, unresolved genuine crash evidence remains protected. Add exact consecutive-success/no-op regression.
  - id: A0-002
    severity: medium
    required: true
    location: "tools/lib/commands/tool_status.sh:107-145 and final root health classification."
    issue: Historical root fallback after completed uninstall reports unmanaged available catalog entry as missing broken until another mutation archives receipts.
    evidence: "Safe audit-sequences has 2 failures with row unmanaged supported missing broken last=uninstall:completed."
    required_result: Report available/unmanaged immediately after success without writes, retain optional last-operation history and true managed missing/broken diagnostics.
